# Linux Security & Administration Lab

## Overview

This repository documents my hands-on Linux security and system administration practice. The lab focuses on foundational Linux administration, and file permissions, system configuration, command-line operations, and basic security practices.

## Objectives

- Build practice Linux systems administration skills
- Practice managing users, groups, and permissions
- Strengthen command-line proficiency
- Apply basic Linux security principles
- Document hands-on technical work for professional development

## Environment 

Ubuntu Linux
Kali Lunix
Virtual machine lab environment

## Skills Practice 

- Linux command-line administration
- User and group management
- File and directory permission
- System navigation and file management
- Process and service management
- Basic system security
- Troubleshooting
- Technical documentation

## Lab Documentation

Hands-on exercises, commands, observations, screenshots, and lessons learned will be documented as the lab develops.

## What I Learned 

This section will be updated throughout the lab to document technical concepts, challenges, troubleshooting steps, and lessons learned.

